mail step

The question allows an echo workaround if SMTP isn't configured.

Where to include it?

Create:

Jenkinsfile

in the root of your GitHub repository.

Pipeline Script — SMTP NOT configured

Since you may not have Jenkins email/SMTP configured, use this version first:

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                checkout scm
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                bat 'python -m py_compile app.py'

                echo 'Build completed. Waiting 15 seconds...'

                sleep time: 15, unit: 'SECONDS'

                milestone 1
            }
        }

        stage('Send Notification') {
            steps {
                echo "To: your-email@example.com"
                echo "Subject: ${env.JOB_NAME} - Build #${env.BUILD_NUMBER}"
                echo "Build URL: ${env.BUILD_URL}"
                echo "Notification sent successfully."
            }
        }
    }
}
If SMTP/email is configured

Replace the Send Notification stage with:

stage('Send Notification') {
    steps {
        mail(
            to: 'your-email@example.com',
            subject: "${env.JOB_NAME} - Build #${env.BUILD_NUMBER}",
            body: "Build completed.\nBuild URL: ${env.BUILD_URL}"
        )
    }
}

Replace:

your-email@example.com
